# DSS plate solution with every AMDX/AMDY term 1..13 non-zero (synthetic;
# coefficients of the size of a real Palomar/UK Schmidt plate solution, the
# 5th-degree term AMD13 included, so wcslib uses its degree-5 TPD form),
# southern declination sign, no approximate WCS at all, and a pixel grid
# reaching 5000 px (13 cm on the plate) from the cutout.
# The grid stops at +-5000 px: at +-6000 px wcslib's iterative inverse of
# the plate polynomial (dis.c disx2p, 30 steps of a separable secant
# scheme) fails to converge at three corners (status 9) where Newton
# iteration returns the grid point (4500, -6000) etc. exactly; that is a
# documented difference (docs/VALIDATION.md) with its own case,
# dss_far_outside_plate.
NOTE DSS plate solution, all 13 terms, degree 5
GRID 1 400 9 1 300 9
GRID -5000 5000 9 -5000 5000 9
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 400
NAXIS2  = 300
CNPIX1  = 9120
CNPIX2  = 4410
XPIXELSZ= 25.28445
YPIXELSZ= 25.28445
PPO3    = 177500.0
PPO6    = 177500.0
PLTRAH  = 5
PLTRAM  = 34
PLTRAS  = 31.94
PLTDECSN= '-       '
PLTDECD = 22
PLTDECM = 0
PLTDECS = 52.2
AMDX1   = 6.7165566279E+01
AMDX2   = 1.8513587312E-02
AMDX3   = -4.3815032712E+01
AMDX4   = -1.2310232101E-05
AMDX5   = 1.5281391001E-05
AMDX6   = -2.2214129003E-05
AMDX7   = -3.8711002135E-04
AMDX8   = 2.4110110037E-06
AMDX9   = -6.1911008122E-08
AMDX10  = 2.2930028134E-06
AMDX11  = 1.1102030201E-07
AMDX12  = -1.0212017106E-08
AMDX13  = 2.7311018101E-09
AMDY1   = 6.7167031235E+01
AMDY2   = -2.0129061902E-02
AMDY3   = 2.1304011803E+01
AMDY4   = -1.6513018011E-05
AMDY5   = -2.1030413102E-05
AMDY6   = 9.1001323019E-06
AMDY7   = -4.1021120903E-04
AMDY8   = 2.3810231019E-06
AMDY9   = 4.4013011903E-08
AMDY10  = 2.2401230109E-06
AMDY11  = -2.0991230811E-08
AMDY12  = 1.2903014403E-08
AMDY13  = -3.1102041118E-09
